{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RFYEpgnFYzpyd92x6FFyPB","type":"tool_result","content":"446\tdef _phase5_split_and_cleanup(\n447\t    files: List[_DrainingFile],\n448\t    per_file_consumed: Dict[str, Set[int]],\n449\t    drain_epoch: str,\n450\t    stats: DrainStats,\n451\t) -> None:\n452\t    \"\"\"For each draining file: unlink if fully consumed; else atomic-split.\n453\t\n454\t    iter2-P0-1: per_file_consumed is a Set[int] of body INDICES. The\n455\t    remainder file is built from the COMPLEMENT (all body indices NOT in\n456\t    the set). This correctly handles out-of-order index consumption (e.g.\n457\t    wall_ns clock-skew rollback where a later body index sorts BEFORE an\n458\t    earlier one and is cut by K_MAX) — prefix-based cleanup would have\n459\t    discarded unprocessed earlier lines.\n460\t\n461\t    iter2-P0-3: SKIP any _DrainingFile whose .quarantined flag is set —\n462\t    the file is already renamed to .malformed.<epoch>; trying to split\n463\t    or unlink the original path would either fail (ENOENT) or, worse,\n464\t    re-sweep the renamed quarantined file on a subsequent drain.\n465\t\n466\t    iter2-P1-3: when splitting, mint a NEW drain_epoch for the destination\n467\t    so dst path != src path. This closes the `.split.tmp` two-step window\n468\t    (old code reused src epoch → dst==src → os.rename(src,dst) no-op AND\n469\t    the temp suffix dance remained). Now: tmp → fsync → rename(tmp,\n470\t    new_dst) atomic; unlink(src). Single window if rename succeeds.\n471\t\n472\t    P2-4: header is written VERBATIM from file.header_raw — no JSON\n473\t    re-encode (preserves byte identity of _spool_uuid sentinel chain).\n474\t    \"\"\"\n475\t    for f in files:\n476\t        # iter2-P0-3: skip quarantined files — original path doesn't exist\n477\t        # at .draining.<epoch> anymore; it was renamed to .malformed.<epoch>.\n478\t        if f.quarantined:\n479\t            continue\n480\t        path_key = str(f.path)\n481\t        if f.header is None and not f.body_lines:\n482\t            # Already empty (no body) — just unlink the (header-only) file.\n483\t            try:\n484\t                if f.path.exists():\n485\t                    os.unlink(str(f.path))\n486\t            except OSError:\n487\t                pass\n488\t            continue\n489\t        consumed_set = per_file_consumed.get(path_key, set())\n490\t        total = len(f.body_lines)\n491\t        # iter2-P0-1: fully consumed iff every body index is in the set.\n492\t        if total == 0 or all(i in consumed_set for i in range(total)):\n493\t            try:\n494\t                os.unlink(str(f.path))\n495\t                stats.files_consumed_fully += 1\n496\t            except OSError as e:\n497\t                _breadcrumb(f\"phase5 unlink failed: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\")\n498\t            continue\n499\t\n500\t        # iter2-P1-3: mint a NEW epoch for the split destination so\n501\t        # dst_path differs from src_path; this collapses the prior\n502\t        # two-step `.split.tmp` rename dance into a single rename+unlink.\n503\t        new_epoch = secrets.token_hex(4)\n504\t        tmp_token = secrets.token_hex(4)\n505\t        # tmp is a sibling .tmp.<token> for atomic create+rename within same dir"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8cec1f7b-b09b-4991-a20f-6e5dfe5185fb","uuid":"b5c91eb1-181b-4707-b133-73d098d2da70","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:15:51.663Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/_spool_writer_parts/drain.py","content":"def _phase5_split_and_cleanup(\n    files: List[_DrainingFile],\n    per_file_consumed: Dict[str, Set[int]],\n    drain_epoch: str,\n    stats: DrainStats,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"For each draining file: unlink if fully consumed; else atomic-split.\n\n    iter2-P0-1: per_file_consumed is a Set[int] of body INDICES. The\n    remainder file is built from the COMPLEMENT (all body indices NOT in\n    the set). This correctly handles out-of-order index consumption (e.g.\n    wall_ns clock-skew rollback where a later body index sorts BEFORE an\n    earlier one and is cut by K_MAX) — prefix-based cleanup would have\n    discarded unprocessed earlier lines.\n\n    iter2-P0-3: SKIP any _DrainingFile whose .quarantined flag is set —\n    the file is already renamed to .malformed.<epoch>; trying to split\n    or unlink the original path would either fail (ENOENT) or, worse,\n    re-sweep the renamed quarantined file on a subsequent drain.\n\n    iter2-P1-3: when splitting, mint a NEW drain_epoch for the destination\n    so dst path != src path. This closes the `.split.tmp` two-step window\n    (old code reused src epoch → dst==src → os.rename(src,dst) no-op AND\n    the temp suffix dance remained). Now: tmp → fsync → rename(tmp,\n    new_dst) atomic; unlink(src). Single window if rename succeeds.\n\n    P2-4: header is written VERBATIM from file.header_raw — no JSON\n    re-encode (preserves byte identity of _spool_uuid sentinel chain).\n    \"\"\"\n    for f in files:\n        # iter2-P0-3: skip quarantined files — original path doesn't exist\n        # at .draining.<epoch> anymore; it was renamed to .malformed.<epoch>.\n        if f.quarantined:\n            continue\n        path_key = str(f.path)\n        if f.header is None and not f.body_lines:\n            # Already empty (no body) — just unlink the (header-only) file.\n            try:\n                if f.path.exists():\n                    os.unlink(str(f.path))\n            except OSError:\n                pass\n            continue\n        consumed_set = per_file_consumed.get(path_key, set())\n        total = len(f.body_lines)\n        # iter2-P0-1: fully consumed iff every body index is in the set.\n        if total == 0 or all(i in consumed_set for i in range(total)):\n            try:\n                os.unlink(str(f.path))\n                stats.files_consumed_fully += 1\n            except OSError as e:\n                _breadcrumb(f\"phase5 unlink failed: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\")\n            continue\n\n        # iter2-P1-3: mint a NEW epoch for the split destination so\n        # dst_path differs from src_path; this collapses the prior\n        # two-step `.split.tmp` rename dance into a single rename+unlink.\n        new_epoch = secrets.token_hex(4)\n        tmp_token = secrets.token_hex(4)\n        # tmp is a sibling .tmp.<token> for atomic create+rename within same dir","numLines":60,"startLine":446,"totalLines":623}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RFYEpgnFYzpyd92x6FFyPB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
